.env.*.local

# READMEs are always tracked — including the per-paper review summaries under
# papers/<year>/<Paper_ID>/README.md. Git resolves a path by the LAST matching
# pattern, so this block must stay at the very bottom of the file: a negation
# placed above a broader pattern is silently overridden by it. Keep new ignore
# rules above this block, and mirror these negations in any nested .gitignore
# that could match a README. Note that a directory-level ignore (e.g.
# `/apn-lib/`) still hides everything inside it — git never descends into it, so
# no negation can rescue a README there. Never ignore a papers/ README that way.
!README.md
!**/README.md
